-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under NIST SP 800-53 CM-2 and COBIT 2019 BAI07, production and development environments must be separated to prevent resource contention. Without isolation, resource-intensive development queries can degrade production database availability and response times for end users.
Wrong (A): Development queries do not typically corrupt production data unless they share the same database instance; the concern here is resource contention on shared hardware, not data corruption.
Wrong (B): Unauthorized data access is a valid concern but secondary to performance degradation when the stated issue is lack of resource isolation on the same physical server.
Wrong (D): Backup schedule conflicts are an operational inconvenience but do not represent the primary risk of collocating production and development on shared hardware without isolation.$EXPL$
