-- Q757: IT Infrastructure and Architecture [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Per NIST SP 800-34, asynchronous replication to a warm standby site achieves sub-hour RPO through replication lag and supports manual failover within a 4-hour RTO. This configuration appropriately balances cost with the stated recovery objectives.
Wrong (A): Nightly tape backups produce an RPO of up to 24 hours and a cold site requires hardware provisioning, yielding an RTO far exceeding 4 hours.
Wrong (B): Synchronous replication with a hot site provides near-zero RPO and near-instant failover, which exceeds the stated requirements and incurs significantly higher cost without corresponding benefit.
Wrong (D): Weekly full backups with daily differentials produce an RPO of up to 24 hours, far exceeding the 1-hour RPO requirement.$EXPL$
